{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), the dominant uncertainty is whether adding the image modality provides meaningful signal in this multimodal cellular profiling task. Config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000 + resnet50, concat) is the cleanest A/B comparison to config_001: it holds the RNA encoder and profile setting constant while introducing the image modality with a standard encoder and the simplest fusion strategy. If accuracy improves substantially, it validates the multimodal direction and justifies further exploration of encoders, aggregation, and fusion. If it does not, it redirects the budget toward improving the RNA-only pipeline (better encoders, multiprofile). This single experiment resolves the most consequential design question in the study and is the highest-information use of the next limited budget slot."
}

